---
description: Frontend rules for pages, components, hooks, and context
globs: ["src/components/**/*.{ts,tsx}", "src/pages/**/*.{ts,tsx}", "src/context/**/*.{ts,tsx}", "src/hooks/**/*.{ts,tsx}"]
---

Frontend rules:
- use TypeScript carefully and prefer explicit types
- keep page components focused on composition and screen logic
- move reusable or heavy logic into hooks, helpers, or services when clearly beneficial
- avoid making page files too large or too stateful
- reuse existing UI patterns and components before creating new ones
- handle loading, empty, error, and success states explicitly
- preserve current UX behavior unless asked to change it
- prefer incremental refactors over introducing a whole new frontend architecture

When refactoring frontend code:
- identify what should stay in the page
- extract only the responsibilities that clearly improve readability or reuse
- keep changes small and easy to review